      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "At the very least disclosure should be a thing. Being able to filter it would be nice but disclosing that something was made with generative tools should probably be implemented as these tools unfortunately gain more and more traction. \n\nI know of at least three major world creators who pad their maps with generative slop and skyboxes and don't disclose it at all. The fact it's so normalized is frankly disappointing since currently none of these tools have proper regulations in place to protect the creators they're scraping from.",
