        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "True markets are informed markets.  That's why nutrition labels are a thing.\n\nI don't believe VRChat can in good conscious say this sort of labelling doesn't matter: AI is the hottest button in content creation, they have a label for way less important things, and Steam does this.\n\nThe only reasons I can think of for not doing this put profits over people: the pure revenue generation from increased monetized output, investor contract requirements, or plans to endorse/create AI content or systems themselves.\n\nIf anyone can think of any reason that doesn't put profits over an informed market, please let me know.  Especially VRChat.  Non-action would speak volumes for itself, though.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
